cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Output consistency of large language models in nursing clinical judgement: data and code"
message: >-
  If you use this dataset or code, please cite both the article and this
  repository.
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Tajima
    given-names: Hiroyuki
    affiliation: "Faculty of Nursing, Shumei University, Japan"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3817-4455"
abstract: >-
  Raw API responses, analysis scripts, scenario texts, item-selection code,
  and figure-generation code for a two-study evaluation of the output
  consistency of three commercial large language models (GPT-4o, Claude Opus
  4.5, Gemini 2.5 Flash-Lite) in nursing clinical judgement. Study 1 uses 30
  author-written English scenarios; Study 2 is an independent cross-lingual
  external validation on 90 publicly released items of the Japanese national
  nursing examination (29,700 API calls). The Nursing Consistency Index (NCI)
  is defined as 1 - H(R) / log2(k), where H(R) is the Shannon entropy of the
  empirical response distribution and k is the number of options.
keywords:
  - large language models
  - output consistency
  - nursing education
  - clinical decision support
  - reproducibility
  - cross-lingual validation
